body:
CC @Ivorforce for the `STATIC_ASSERT_INCOMPLETE_TYPE` warning.

The actual warning:
```
In file included from ./scene/resources/material.h:35,
                 from ./scene/resources/mesh.h:36,
                 from ./scene/debugger/scene_debugger.h:40,
                 from scene/main/node.cpp:48:
./scene/resources/shader.h:39:7: error: defining 'Shader', which previously failed to be complete in a SFINAE context [-Werror=sfinae-incomplete=]
   39 | class Shader : public Resource {
      |       ^~~~~~
./core/typedefs.h:454:49: note: here.  Use '-Wsfinae-incomplete=2' for a diagnostic at that point
  454 | struct is_fully_defined<T, std::void_t<decltype(sizeof(T))>> : std::true_type {};
      |                                                 ^~~~~~~~~
```

Not a warning, but a straight-up error with `_FORCE_INLINE_` and `_ALWAYS_INLINE_` happens when trying to compile with `optimize=debug dev_build=no`.

`__attribute__((always_inline)) inline` throws an error if the function isn't considered for inlining:

```
In file included from ./core/templates/cowdata.h:34,
                 from ./core/string/ustring.h:34,
                 from ./core/string/string_name.h:33,
                 from ./core/core_string_names.h:33,
                 from ./core/variant/variant.h:33,
                 from ./core/object/property_info.h:34,
                 from ./core/object/method_info.h:33,
                 from ./core/object/gdtype.h:33,
                 from ./core/object/object.h:34,
                 from ./core/config/project_settings.h:33,
                 from platform/linuxbsd/crash_handler_linuxbsd.cpp:33:
In function 'void* operator new(size_t, void* (*)(size_t))',
    inlined from 'List<T, A>::Element* List<T, A>::push_back(const T&) [with T = String; A = DefaultAllocator]' at ./core/templates/list.h:289:12:
./core/os/memory.h:103:37: error: inlining failed in call to 'always_inline' 'static void* DefaultAllocator::alloc(size_t)': function not considered for inlining
  103 |         _FORCE_INLINE_ static void *alloc(size_t p_memory) { return Memory::alloc_static(p_memory, false); }
      |                                     ^~~~~
./core/os/memory.h:114:27: note: called from here
  114 |         return p_allocfunc(p_size);
      |                ~~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~
In function 'void* operator new(size_t, void* (*)(size_t))',
    inlined from 'List<T, A>::Element* List<T, A>::push_back(const T&) [with T = String; A = DefaultAllocator]' at ./core/templates/list.h:295:16:
./core/os/memory.h:103:37: error: inlining failed in call to 'always_inline' 'static void* DefaultAllocator::alloc(size_t)': function not considered for inlining
  103 |         _FORCE_INLINE_ static void *alloc(size_t p_memory) { return Memory::alloc_static(p_memory, false); }
      |                                     ^~~~~
./core/os/memory.h:114:27: note: called from here
  114 |         return p_allocfunc(p_size);
      |                ~~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~
```

Doesn't happen with `optimize=none`, `optimize=debug dev_build=yes` or omitting `optimize` at all.
